# Zamba2-1.2B-style (Zyphra, 2024): a Mamba-2 backbone that calls one shared transformer
# block before every sixth Mamba-2 layer. "shared" makes a definition a single module
# instead of a template, so all six uses of `sa` have the same parameters. The block has
# no residual of its own: its output, through a linear layer of each call's own, is
# added to the input of the Mamba-2 layer after it.
#
# Simplified: Zamba2 feeds the block the stream concatenated with the embedding, and
# gives each call LoRA adapters on q, k, v and the MLP; here it reads the stream alone.
d_model    = 2048
vocab_size = 32000

norm = rmsnorm(eps=1e-5)
ssm  = mamba2(state_size=128)
# Heads as wide as on Zamba2's 4096-wide input, with logits scaled as if half as wide.
attn = gqa(num_heads=32, num_kv_heads=32, head_dim=128, scale=0.125, rope=rope())
ffn  = gated_mlp(intermediate_size=8192, activation=gelu)

m = [norm ssm]
shared sa = norm attn norm ffn
h = [(_ + sa linear(features=d_model)) norm ssm]

model = embed (m^5 h)^6 m^2 norm head(tied=true)
